# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ashraq environment
#
# EVERY VARIABLE BELOW IS OPTIONAL. The application is fully functional with no
# environment file at all — that is a deliberate design requirement, not a
# limitation. With no key configured, all six AI routes serve deterministic,
# engine-derived responses and the app is completely demoable.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Groq free tier — https://console.groq.com/keys (no credit card required).
# Set this to upgrade the AI panels from deterministic templates to live model
# output. Nothing else changes; no code edit is needed.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT CURRENTLY USED — documented for the record.
#
# The global rate limiter (lib/ai/rate-limit.ts) is an in-memory token bucket,
# which means it resets on each serverless cold start and is therefore
# best-effort rather than a durable global guarantee. The spec-compliant fix is
# Upstash Redis via @upstash/ratelimit. The seam in rate-limit.ts is kept clean
# so this is a single-function swap. See README "Known limitations".
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
